## Symbolic Memory

Facts may be forgotten.

Symbols may trigger reconstruction.

Examples include:

- flags,
- emblems,
- names,
- archetypes,
- myths,
- rituals,
- and stories.

Symbolic memory functions as a recovery mechanism.

---

## Poetic Memory

Poetry preserves meaning differently from technical language.

Technical language prioritizes precision.

Poetry prioritizes resonance.

Technical language explains.

Poetry reminds.

The ecosystem values both.

---

